<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka 3-month T-bill yields sharply down.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka 3-month T-bill yields sharply down.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lankan treasury bill yields weakened further with weighted average of three, six and 12-month bills falling by 1.33 percentage points, 0.78 and 0.87 respectively, at Wednesday's auction, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		   bids received   bids accepted   avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     5,866	     1,525	  15.16 (16.49)</p>
<p>    6 months     2,336	     1,000	  15.78 (16.56)</p>
<p>    12 months    4,214	     2,559	  15.80 (16.67)</p>
<p>    Total	 12,416	     5,084</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets).</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
